From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Restyle only what a loaded @import's rules can match

A loaded @import forced every stylesheet origin dirty, which restyles and
relays out the whole document. On the ECMAScript spec the two highlight.js
theme imports, one of them behind a dark-scheme media query that never
matches, each cost about 800 ms of full restyle and relayout after the
first layout.

Report the load to stylo as a rule insertion against the owning document
sheet, the way Gecko handles an import load. Stylo skips imports whose media
does not match and invalidates by selector otherwise. An import that is not
found under a document sheet, such as one inside a shadow root, keeps the old
full invalidation.
---
 src/document.rs | 122 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 118 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/document.rs b/src/document.rs
index c5955e3..dc4d2a9 100644
--- a/src/document.rs
+++ b/src/document.rs
@@ -62,8 +62,12 @@ use style::{
